    "salt": "7idPsej34qhHihboKJyeeQ==",
    "text": "Bres is an Irish god. Several figures share this name. The chief one was Bres mac Elatha. He was originally called Eochu. His beauty earned him the nickname Bres, meaning the beautiful one. His mother was the Tuatha Dé Danann princess Ériu or Eithne. His father was the Fomorian king Elatha. As king of Tara he held back fire and gave guests only plain crackers. He even denied drink to a bard. Cairbre mac Éadoine answered with a sharp satire. Boils broke out on Bres's face. A blemished king could not rule. The people drove him from the throne. He joined his father's forces and lost the second battle of Mag Tuired. In some accounts his consort was the goddess Brigit. Their son Ruadán died at Mag Tuired. Another Bres fell in the first battle of Mag Tuired. A Bres also rules Hy-Brâzil, an island of the Otherworld.",
